## cc-thinking-skills (tjboudreaux)

The `## Form and check a hypothesis` section of `references/local-feedback.md`
adapts material from `tjboudreaux/cc-thinking-skills` at commit
`7b8fece345dfaa11773be7152ccd194589cb5437`, specifically these upstream paths:
[thinking-scientific-method](https://github.com/tjboudreaux/cc-thinking-skills/blob/7b8fece345dfaa11773be7152ccd194589cb5437/skills/thinking-scientific-method/SKILL.md),
[thinking-kepner-tregoe](https://github.com/tjboudreaux/cc-thinking-skills/blob/7b8fece345dfaa11773be7152ccd194589cb5437/skills/thinking-kepner-tregoe/SKILL.md), and
[thinking-five-whys-plus](https://github.com/tjboudreaux/cc-thinking-skills/blob/7b8fece345dfaa11773be7152ccd194589cb5437/skills/thinking-five-whys-plus/SKILL.md).
The section is rewritten in jstack's terms; several sentences follow upstream
closely.

Upstream reports a provisional +4.0pp fault-localization delta for an earlier scientific-method body (sha256 9a7a94d3…) against an active placebo; not elevated (AUDIT.md §5.1). The pinned body (fc0440ed…) was not measured upstream. kepner-tregoe −1.8pp no-lift, five-whys-plus +1.5pp not significant. All upstream skills are manual-only. jstack has not measured this adaptation.

